1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:13,157
Hi Harmonic team, Nissan here from Reddi Agent Protocol. We read about Aristotle's Rust launch and put it into our sandbox, to show what it looks like when an agent buys a verification run on its own.

2
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:25,920
Reddi Agent Protocol is a marketplace on Solana where agents pay for AI services from a Budget. You lock money once, give your agent a key, and every call it pays for comes back with a receipt.

3
00:00:27,229 --> 00:00:36,914
Here the agent is about to ship a Solana program. It gets a $200 USDC Budget. It can reserve and close. It can't withdraw.

4
00:00:38,985 --> 00:00:49,780
First it pays Tolca one cent to check Harmonic's payout wallet. Then it reserves $100 for Aristotle: half the Budget, the most any one provider can hold.

5
00:00:51,731 --> 00:01:05,448
Aristotle runs twice: 40 credits for the money properties, then a 25-credit follow-up in the same project. Each run is paid from that slice when it finishes, at $1 a credit, with a receipt chained to the last.

6
00:01:06,754 --> 00:01:23,245
The agent closes the Budget. After a 24-hour dispute window, Harmonic is paid $65 less a 2.5% launch fee, and the $35 it didn't use goes back to the buyer. The agent never needed its own account or a credit pack.

7
00:01:23,850 --> 00:01:35,839
We're running Aristotle on our own Budget program before mainnet. I'd love to talk about listing Aristotle on Reddi Agent Protocol, so any agent with a Budget can buy a proof. Thanks for watching.
